+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "  maxTurns: 5,",
+  "cause": "The customer-facing `triage` agent is defined without a `store`, so Genkit treats it as client-managed and rejects any `sessionId` resume with FAILED_PRECONDITION, forcing the customer to repeat the order number.",
+  "evidence": "Before the fix, `triage.chat({ sessionId })` threw \"FAILED_PRECONDITION: Cannot use 'sessionId' with agent 'triage': this agent has no store configured\" while `refundAgent`, which has `store`, resumed fine. After adding `store,` to `triage`, the two-turn conversation under one sessionId answered \"Your order A-1001 has been shipped. The ETA is 2026-10-22 and the tracking code is NW-7F3K2Q.\" and then \"Your order A-1001 has been shipped.\" for the follow-up."
+}
